CPU SNAP regression with three non-collinear atoms, twojmax=2, nonzero
angular coefficients, and nonzero quadratic coefficients. The synthetic
potential is for software testing only. Energy, force, and stress are
cross-checked against LAMMPS SNAP using the same cell and coordinates.

LAMMPS (30 Mar 2026 development build, c46bbef) gives total potential energy
54.909561 eV, forces (eV/Angstrom) of (67.292804, 57.547644, 0),
(-92.139945, 60.594450, 0), and (24.847141, -118.142093, 0), and Pxx
-122909.08 bar. ABACUS reports stress in kbar. The calculator unit test
checks each force component and compares virial with an energy strain derivative.

Model files: ../../SIMULATION_MODELS/snap_105.coeff and
../../SIMULATION_MODELS/snap_105.param.
